{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The current crate is not an independent Rust implementation: `build.rs` recompiles all 25 C translation units under renamed symbols, and Rust exports naked jump trampolines to them. That explains the broad ABI coverage but also means differential tests may only prove C against the same C; I’ll still execute the required gates exactly and flag this architectural fact separately from byte-parity results. First I’m running the mandated compile check."}}
